<!--
Xbox One S controller over USB.

Driver: xpad (kernel). Name from the xpad device table, version = bcdDevice of the
USB device (usb_to_input_id). The first Xbox One pads (045e:02d1, 045e:02dd) are
not covered; they get the ES wizard.

Buttons (SDL joystick index = evdev key codes in ascending order, BTN_JOYSTICK and up first):
  A (south) 0, B (east) 1, X (west) 2, Y (north) 3, LB 4, RB 5, Back 6, Start 7,
  Guide 8, left stick 9, right stick 10.
Axes: left stick 0/1, LT 2, right stick 3/4, RT 5. D-pad: hat 0.

deviceName is the SDL joystick name, as EmulationStation writes it. ES looks for
the GUID first and then for deviceName (InputManager::loadInputConfig), so the
name is the fallback when the version in the GUID differs (spec section 9).
The CRC in the GUID is computed from the kernel name (see guid-source).
SDL names 045e:02ea "Xbox One S Controller" (controller_list.h).

GUID with CRC (SDL 2.26 and newer, also sdl2-compat on SDL3 in trixie) and without CRC
(older SDL), computed with "emulationstation-web guid" from these values:
guid-source: bus=0x03 vendor=0x045e product=0x02ea version=0x0517 name="Microsoft X-Box One S pad"

UNVERIFIED - check on hardware: The version is the controller firmware (seen: 0x0301, 0x0408, 0x050f,
  0x0511, 0x0515, 0x0517). 0x0517 is the newest value seen. Other firmware: only
  the name match works.
UNVERIFIED - check on hardware: ES writes the SDL name "Xbox One S Controller" (not the kernel name) as deviceName
  on trixie (SDL 3.2 with sdl2-compat).

Sources:
  https://github.com/raspberrypi/linux/blob/rpi-6.18.y/drivers/input/joystick/xpad.c
  https://github.com/libsdl-org/SDL/tree/release-3.2.10/src/joystick (linux/SDL_sysjoystick.c, SDL_joystick.c, controller_list.h, SDL_gamepad_db.h)
  https://github.com/mdqinc/SDL_GameControllerDB (gamecontrollerdb.txt, Linux GUIDs seen in the wild)
  https://github.com/RetroPie/EmulationStation/blob/stable/es-core/src/InputManager.cpp
-->
